 "literal": "Wife they-who-desire excellent benefit they-attain-not; action they-who-desire rejecting thing-also that.",
 "translation": "Those who lust after their wives will not attain excellent benefits; that is also a thing rejected by those who desire great action.",
 "modern": "மனைவியின் மீது அதீத ஆசை கொண்டவர்கள் சிறந்த பயன்களை அடைய மாட்டார்கள். செயலில் வெற்றி பெற விரும்புபவர்கள் வெறுத்து ஒதுக்கும் பொருளும் அந்த பெண்ணாசையே ஆகும்.",
 "explanation": "This couplet warns against letting infatuation with one's wife override one's duties. The word 'maṉai' (household) here stands metonymically for the wife, and 'viḻaivār' refers to those who excessively desire or lust after her. Such people cannot achieve 'māṇ payaṉ' (excellent benefits or glorious results) in life. Furthermore, the text notes that this kind of infatuation ('atu') is exactly the thing rejected ('vēṇṭā poruḷ') by those who are committed to meaningful action ('viṉai viḻaiyār').",
